## 🛠 Quick Implementation Guide

### Step 1: Immediate Security (Do Today)

```bash
# 1. Remove exposed secrets
git rm --cached .env.test
echo ".env*" >> .gitignore
echo "!.env.example" >> .gitignore

# 2. Create safe environment template
cp .env.example .env.development

# 3. Commit changes
git add .gitignore .env.example
git commit -m "Remove secrets, add environment templates"

# 4. ROTATE ALL CREDENTIALS IMMEDIATELY
# - Change database password
# - Revoke AWS keys, create new ones
# - Regenerate API keys
```

### Step 2: Install Security Dependencies

```bash
npm install express helmet cors express-rate-limit morgan jsonwebtoken dotenv express-validator
npm install --save-dev nodemon jest supertest
```

### Step 3: Update app.js

```javascript
require('dotenv').config();
const helmet = require('helmet');
const cors = require('cors');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

const app = express();

// Security middleware
app.use(helmet());
app.use(cors({ origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS.split(',') }));
app.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, max: 100 }));

// Authentication
function authenticateToken(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization']?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'No token' });

  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {
    if (err) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid token' });
    req.user = user;
    next();
  });
}

// Routes
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
});

app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  res.json({ users: [/* data */] });
});

// Error handling
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });
});

app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000);
```

### Step 4: Configure Environment

**Create .env.development:**
```
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-key
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
```

**Create .env (local only, never commit):**
```
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
JWT_SECRET=your-strong-random-secret-key-here
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/db
```

---

## 📝 Minimum Secure Code Template

```javascript
require('dotenv').config();
const express = require('express');
const helmet = require('helmet');
const cors = require('cors');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

const app = express();

// Middleware
app.use(helmet());
app.use(cors());
app.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, max: 100 }));
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));

// Authentication
const auth = (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers['authorization']?.split(' ')[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).send('No token');
  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (e, user) => {
    if (e) return res.status(403).send('Invalid');
    req.user = user;
    next();
  });
};

// Routes
app.get('/health', (req, res) => res.json({ ok: true }));
app.get('/users', auth, (req, res) => res.json([/* data */]));

// Error handler
app.use((e, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(e);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Server error' });
});

app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000);
```

---

## 🔐 Environment Variables Checklist

Required for production:

```
✓ NODE_ENV=production
✓ PORT=3000
✓ JWT_SECRET=<strong-random-value>
✓ ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
✓ DATABASE_URL=postgres://...
✓ (Any API keys needed for your app)
```

**Never store in code:**
- ✗ Database credentials
- ✗ API keys
- ✗ JWT secrets
- ✗ Encryption keys
- ✗ Third-party tokens

---

## 🧪 Testing Your Security

```bash
# Run tests
npm test

# Check dependencies
npm audit

# Lint code
npm run lint

# Local security test
curl http://localhost:3000/health

# Test with auth token
TOKEN=$(curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login -d '{"username":"demo"}' | jq -r '.token')
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:3000/users
```

---

## 📋 Deployment Checklist

Before going to production:

```
[ ] npm audit - no vulnerabilities
[ ] All env vars set
[ ] HTTPS enabled
[ ] JWT_SECRET is random (min 32 chars)
[ ] Rate limiting configured
[ ] Error handling tested
[ ] Authentication working
[ ] CORS properly configured
[ ] Logs configured and working
[ ] Database credentials secure
[ ] Secrets not in git history
[ ] .gitignore includes .env
[ ] package-lock.json committed
```

---

## 🚀 Deploy Safe Command

```bash
# Verify security before deployment
npm audit --audit-level=moderate && \
npm run lint && \
npm test && \
echo "✓ Security checks passed!"

# Deploy to production
export NODE_ENV=production
npm start
```

---

## 🆘 Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ **WRONG:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // No auth check!
  res.json(allUsers);
});

const secret = "hardcoded-secret"; // Don't hardcode!
```

✅ **RIGHT:**
```javascript
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  // Auth required!
  res.json(allUsers);
});

const secret = process.env.JWT_SECRET; // From environment
```

---

❌ **WRONG:**
```javascript
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server started');
});
// No error handling!
```

✅ **RIGHT:**
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err);
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Server error' });
});

app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000);
```

---

❌ **WRONG:**
```
DATABASE_PASSWORD=super-secret
API_KEY=12345
.env (committed to git!)
```

✅ **RIGHT:**
```
# .env.example (committed - no real values!)
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your-password-here
API_KEY=your-key-here

# .env (NOT committed, added to .gitignore)
DATABASE_PASSWORD=actual-password
API_KEY=actual-key
```

---

## 📚 Learn More

- [Node.js Security](https://nodejs.org/en/docs/guides/security/)
- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/Top10/)
- [Express Security Best Practices](https://expressjs.com/en/advanced/best-practice-security.html)
- [CWE Top 25](https://cwe.mitre.org/top25/)

---

## 🎯 Success Criteria

Your app is secure when:

✓ No credentials in git  
✓ All endpoints protected or rate-limited  
✓ HTTPS enforced  
✓ Security headers set  
✓ Input validated  
✓ Errors handled safely  
✓ Dependencies audited  
✓ Logs configured  
✓ Environment variables used  
✓ Tests passing  

