## 🟡 MEDIUM: Missing Security Headers

### Severity: MEDIUM
### CVSS Score: 5.3 (Medium)
### CWE: CWE-693 - Protection Mechanism Failure

### The Problem

```javascript
// Current app.js does NOT set any security headers
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([...]); // Response headers are minimal/unsafe
});
```

### Response Headers Analysis

```bash
# Current headers:
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

# Missing critical security headers:
- Content-Security-Policy
- X-Frame-Options
- X-Content-Type-Options
- Strict-Transport-Security
- X-XSS-Protection
- Referrer-Policy
- Permissions-Policy
```

### Attack Scenarios

#### 1. Clickjacking Attack
```html
<!-- Attacker's website -->
<iframe src="https://yourapp.com/users?action=delete"></iframe>
<!-- Without X-Frame-Options, this works! -->
```

**Prevention:** X-Frame-Options: DENY

#### 2. MIME Sniffing
```javascript
// Attacker serves file as JSON but browser interprets as HTML
res.json({ data: '<script>alert("XSS")</script>' });
// Without X-Content-Type-Options, browser might execute it
```

**Prevention:** X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

#### 3. XSS Attack
```html
<!-- Reflected XSS without Content-Security-Policy -->
<img src=x onerror="alert('XSS')">
```

**Prevention:** Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'

### Solution

```javascript
const helmet = require('helmet');
const app = express();

app.use(helmet()); // Adds all recommended security headers

// Or manually configure:
app.use(helmet({
  contentSecurityPolicy: {
    directives: {
      defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
      scriptSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"],
      styleSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"],
      imgSrc: ["'self'", 'data:', 'https:'],
    },
  },
  frameGuard: { action: 'deny' },
  noSniff: true,
  xssFilter: true,
  hsts: {
    maxAge: 31536000,
    includeSubDomains: true,
    preload: true
  }
}));
```

