## 🟡 MEDIUM: No Rate Limiting

### Severity: MEDIUM
### CVSS Score: 5.9 (Medium)
### CWE: CWE-770 - Allocation of Resources Without Limits

### The Problem

```javascript
// Current app.js has NO rate limiting
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([...]); // Anyone can call this unlimited times
});
```

### Attack Scenarios

#### 1. Denial of Service (DOS)
```bash
# Attacker floods the server
for i in {1..10000}; do
  curl https://yourapp.com/users &
done

# Server becomes unresponsive for legitimate users
```

#### 2. Brute Force Attack
```bash
# Try to guess passwords/tokens
for password in $(cat /usr/share/dict/words); do
  curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $password" https://yourapp.com/api/secret
done
```

#### 3. API Abuse
```bash
# Expensive operation called unlimited times
for i in {1..1000}; do
  curl https://yourapp.com/ai-analyze?text="longtext" &
done

# Costs spike unexpectedly
```

### Request Timeline (Current)
```
Time 0ms:   Request 1 accepted
Time 1ms:   Request 2 accepted
Time 2ms:   Request 3 accepted
...
Time 100ms: Request 100 accepted
Time 101ms: Request 101 accepted  ← Server overloaded!
...
Time 500ms: Server crashes → No one can access app
```

### Solution

```javascript
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const RedisStore = require('rate-limit-redis');
const redis = require('redis');

// Simple in-memory rate limiter
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100,                   // 100 requests per window
  message: 'Too many requests from this IP',
  standardHeaders: true,      // Return RateLimit info in headers
  legacyHeaders: false        // Disable X-RateLimit-* headers
});

// Apply to all routes
app.use(limiter);

// Or specific routes with stricter limits
const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 5, // Only 5 attempts per 15 minutes
  skipSuccessfulRequests: true // Don't count successful attempts
});

app.post('/login', loginLimiter, (req, res) => {
  // Prevent brute force attacks
});

// Production: Use Redis-backed rate limiter
const redisClient = redis.createClient();

const advancedLimiter = rateLimit({
  store: new RedisStore({
    client: redisClient,
    prefix: 'rl:' // Rate limit prefix
  }),
  windowMs: 60 * 1000, // 1 minute
  max: 30
});
```

### Request Timeline (With Rate Limiting)
```
Time 0ms:   Request 1 accepted
Time 1ms:   Request 2 accepted
...
Time 100ms: Request 100 accepted
Time 101ms: Request 101 REJECTED (rate limit exceeded)
Time 102ms: Request 102 REJECTED
...
Time 15min: Counter resets
Time 15min 1ms: Request 101 accepted ← Normal operation resumes
```

