## Loading Different Configuration Files

### Using dotenv-cli (Recommended)
```bash
# Development
dotenv -e .env.development node app.js

# Staging
dotenv -e .env.staging node app.js

# Production
dotenv -e .env.production node app.js
```

Install dotenv-cli:
```bash
npm install --save-dev dotenv-cli
```

### Using npm Scripts

Add to `package.json`:
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node app.js",
    "start:dev": "dotenv -e .env.development nodemon app.js",
    "start:staging": "dotenv -e .env.staging node app.js",
    "start:prod": "dotenv -e .env.production node app.js"
  }
}
```

Then run:
```bash
npm run start:dev      # Development
npm run start:staging  # Staging
npm run start:prod     # Production
```

