const PORT = config.get('server.port');
```

### Docker/Kubernetes (secrets)
```bash
docker run -e DB_PASSWORD=$(cat /run/secrets/db_password) myapp
```

---

## Summary

| Hardcoded Value | Solution | Priority |
|-----------------|----------|----------|
| Port 3000 | `process.env.PORT` | CRITICAL |
| Host (localhost) | `process.env.HOST` | HIGH |
| Mock user data | Config file or database | CRITICAL |
| NODE_ENV | Set explicitly | HIGH |
| Status messages | Dynamic based on NODE_ENV | MEDIUM |

---

## Testing

Test that environment variables work:

```bash
